Translation patch: `ParsedNamedParams::parse` (the state-machine loop)

Change: `for (i, c) in query.iter().enumerate() { <body> }` becomes `let mut i = 0; while i < query.len() { state = parse_step(state, query[i], i, &mut have_positional, &mut cur_param, &mut params); i += 1; }`, where the new function `parse_step` is the old loop body verbatim except that `c` is the byte (`u8`) instead of a `&u8` (so `*c`/`*x` become `c`/`x`), `have_positional`/`cur_param` are reached through `&mut`, and it returns the new `state`.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Enumerate` or the slice iterator (see patches 04/05/27), and on the index loop with the body inline it fails with "Could not compute a loop fixed point in 2 iterations"; with the body in a function the loop translates.
Behaviour: Identical: the same bytes are visited in the same order with the same index, and the step performs the same reads and writes of `state`, `have_positional`, `cur_param` and `params` (comparing `u8` values instead of `&u8` references is the same comparison).

